      "researcher_notes": "EXISTENCE/CLASSIFICATION: real, well-documented pipeline. It is the short marine loading line connecting El Hamra petroleum port (New Alamein, Matruh Governorate) to an offshore tanker-loading buoy ('Shamandoura'), built/operated by WEPCO (Western Desert Operating Petroleum Co). Three independent sources, two of them primary, all agree on the core facts: (1) presidency.eg (Egyptian Presidency's own site, dated Aug 2020) states the line is 8 km long, 36 inches in diameter, raises shipping capacity to 1,000,000 bpd of crude, at a cost of ~$100 million; (2) WEPCO's own official Arabic project page ('مشروع إنشاء الشمندورة البحرية رقم 2 و خط الشحن البحري 36 بوصة', published 2023) independently states an 8 km, 36-inch line built for crude loading, contractor PMS, consultant Enppi, work completed 2019; (3) Reuters via Ahram Online (19 Aug 2020, verified via Wayback after the live URL 403'd) reports Egypt 'brought online' the '8-kilometre Hamra-Shamandoura loading pipeline', raising al-Hamra's shipping capacity to 1 million bpd, and names WEPCO as operator. All three name this exact pipeline (not a generic/aggregate reference) so this is not a GEM-only entity. DUPLICATE check against the 46-pipeline Egypt-oil roster: no other row describes this El Hamra<->offshore-buoy loading line; P3693 ('El Hamra-Sidi Krir-Alexandria Oil Pipeline', 90 km/16in) is a different, larger onshore line from the same port and is not a duplicate. CLASSIFICATION: correctly Fuel=Oil (crude); this is a legitimate port-to-buoy crude loading line, comparable to other GEM terminal-loading segments. Two of the three source pages ultimately trace to the same underlying event (Egyptian Cabinet's Aug 2020 announcement, per Ahram's own text: 'the cabinet said in a statement'), but the Egyptian Presidency's site and WEPCO's own project page are each themselves primary/regulatory-class sources (government and operator respectively) rather than press reprints of each other, so the corroboration is treated as high tier per the confidence-tier rubric ('one primary/regulatory source' suffices, and here there are two independent primary sources plus the wire report). The gem.wiki page's three cited sources (almalnews.com, ahram.org.eg, wepco-eg.com/wepco/vision-mission/) are now ALL dead on the live web (almalnews 404, ahram 403-blocked live but its Wayback capture is readable and confirms the facts, wepco vision-mission 404 with a Wayback capture that exists per CDX but is currently unreadable due to web.archive.org content-serving being intermittently unreachable from this session — existence-only, not cited). Two better, currently-live primary sources (presidency.eg and a different, still-live WEPCO project page) were substituted in their place.",
